+
+# HarmonyOS application graph: synthetic HAP path hints
+
+## Question and carriers
+
+The C2 question was whether `project-harmony-application-graph` can consume an authenticated `inspect-artifact` inventory for a minimal HAP and report Stage/FA packaging hints. Only synthetic carriers were exercised; these runs do not establish behavior on a shipped HarmonyOS application, HSP, App Pack, or device.
+
+The retained, exact ZIP bytes are `carriers/stage.hap` (548 bytes, SHA-256 `21d46dbc88ba8f8c1306a70f727d8ee0383dc37c19430463dc7849f557c4a65f`) and `carriers/fa.hap` (604 bytes, SHA-256 `9cb84d18fade6e7653d90a15d01d18179f9f47fb92187954dfbdf75bff6c2457`). `carrier-recipe.json` records each exact member byte string as base64, member hashes/lengths, order, ZIP_STORED method, fixed DOS timestamp, Unix file mode and Python version; the full carrier files are also retained. Stage contains `module.json` declaring module `entry` and one `EntryAbility`, `resources.index`, and `ets/modules.abc`. FA contains `config.json` with a module and one `EntryAbility`, plus the same resource and placeholder bytecode entries.
+
+## Observations
+
+- `inspect-artifact` on Stage exited 0: outer Evidence `ev_7c80b736aa635c44a0ea222bb6db2f1540d0f8bac65bd9c280c1efbc76fbe52e`; nested `inventory_artifact` Evidence `ev_ae4600c27ed4b6ed50dccafeb3983157577ab59835d2d0d21c9876e4ab25031b`, root format `hap`, root SHA-256 as above, 4 nodes/4 occurrences, and `coverage_status: complete`. `project-harmony-application-graph` exited 0: Evidence `ev_a437cf77ed5381ee7e71d36a87a7407bd5f38cb911a2432e8eb69ff554a74820`, projection id `hmp_a9fd23092c373ec51ff385d2936c5c1e2631d8fc33dccc7e1fbd0916f81954f6`, `packaging_model: stage`, and `coverage.status: complete-within-inventory` with `inventory_complete: true`. It classified `module.json` as manifest, `ets/modules.abc` as bytecode, `resources.index` as resource; runtime-family hint was `ark`; native libraries, JavaScript, signing, unavailable components and bridge candidates were empty.
+- `inspect-artifact` on FA exited 0: outer Evidence `ev_9f377f35879ed711cb983a6bc0fe90b7baaa0dafe8eebac20145ff96ca512ba5`; nested `inventory_artifact` Evidence `ev_6fb3f68a68d59baedb0850eced6cc7217514f241ebec689934f3e47877d44fbe`, root format `hap`, root SHA-256 as above, 4 nodes/4 occurrences and complete container-entry coverage. Projection exited 0: Evidence `ev_ac0c26dccd8db383f2ac848cab213e3a375e4b261072b57f52c037c45a32ab92`, projection id `hmp_de45de4cf1017c5fc7a6cc14513c3b440a9d0e3d0b39dfdd7f0e801397737326`, `packaging_model: fa`, and `complete-within-inventory`/`inventory_complete: true`. It classified `config.json`, `ets/modules.abc`, and `resources.index` respectively as manifest, bytecode, and resource; runtime-family hint was `ark`; the same empty component groups and zero bridge candidates were returned.
+
+The two first projection attempts were `invalid_request` (exit 1): the input had been reconstructed from the default presentation output rather than JSON, and carried `limitations[1]` as a key instead of the required `limitations` array. Those attempts and exact payload snapshots are retained in `project-stage/` and `project-fa/`. Re-running both inspections with `--json`, then passing each actual nested inventory Evidence unchanged, produced the successful projections above. The successful inputs are retained at `project-stage/input.json` and `project-fa/input.json`.
+
+## Interpretation and unknowns
+
+**Observation:** the exercised verb pair accepted both synthetic `hap` inventories and produced separate `stage` and `fa` hints with complete inventory coverage for the ZIP central-directory entries. The CLI run does not establish the package formats' semantic validity.
+
+**Inference:** the hints are path-presence classifications, not manifest parsing: the installed source chooses Stage when a manifest path ends in `module.json`, otherwise FA when one ends in `config.json` (`harmonyApplication.js:110-117`). Therefore `stage`/`fa` does not verify module declarations, ability metadata, or HarmonyOS package validity. The source explicitly states that the projection reports paths/hashes without manifest, module, resource or signing semantics (`:62-66`).
+
+**Unknown:** the `.abc` payload is an intentionally invalid text placeholder; the `ark` family is inferred from its suffix and is not proof of Ark bytecode. Resource contents were not decoded. Empty signing entries do not establish unsigned status (a ZIP signing block is outside central-directory inventory). No runtime behavior, valid device installation, N-API declaration/call, App Pack child recursion, HSP behavior, or `.har` shared-library identification was exercised. The zero bridge candidates are only the path-pair result for these two small inventories. `complete-within-inventory` means complete central-directory entry inventory, not semantic package completeness or whole-file coverage beyond that inventory.
+
+The `--schema` call reports `project-harmony-application-graph` input as one `inputJson` argument and `inspect-artifact` input as a `path` argument; those exact outputs are retained under `schema-project/` and `schema-inspect/`. The implementation/source citations and the command results together support this bounded holding; the schema alone is not evidence of successful capability.
